WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.639 --> 00:00:07.640
George R.R. Martin: You know, I'm notorious
for my love of grey characters and one of

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:13.890
the greyest characters in the entire Westeros
is Daemon Targaryen, the Rogue Prince.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:17.310
We took one of the sidebars and made a seperate
story out of it, the Rogue Prince.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:22.820
Daemon is the younger brother of King Viserys
I, for a time he was the heir to the throne

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.910
when Viserys had no children, and then Viserys
started having children and he stopped being

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:29.089
the heir to the throne.

00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:33.260
He's a notorious bad boy, a rogue in every
sense of the word.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:39.660
He was a rival for Viserys' sister and his
own niece Rhaenyra and then later he became

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.120
the husband of Rhaenyra.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.870
He swtiches sides several times, you never
know what side he's going to come down on.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:53.930
He's a very colorful and unpredictable character
and I think he has to rank up there as my

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:54.930
favorite.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.220
Viserys Targaryen: When ravens carried the
news of Aegon's coronation to Dragonstone,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.739
Princess Rhaenyra summoned her own Black Council.

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:07.090
With her was her uncle and husband, Daemon
Targaryen, considered by many to be the most

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:08.530
dangerous man in Westeros.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:14.140
Robert Baratheon: Arrax was struggling to
stay aloft in the gale when a roar shook the

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.140
very foundations of Storm's End.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:23.180
Aemond rose through the clouds and below him
the monstrous Vhagar.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:28.960
Vhagar was five times the size of Arrax and
a hardened survivor of a hundred battles.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.909
Vhagar caught him above Shipbreaker Bay.

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:39.469
Watchers on the castle walls saw distant blasts
of flame and heard a shriek drown out the

00:01:39.469 --> 00:01:40.469
thunder.

00:01:40.469 --> 00:01:44.729
Prince Lucerys fell, broken, to be swallowed
by the waves.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:52.930
With his death, the war of ravens came to
an end, and the war of fire and blood began.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:02:00.030
Catelyn Stark: When Rhaenyra heard of her
son's death, she collapsed.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:06.080
She considered ending the war right then until
a raven arrived from her husband, Daemon.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.780
Her son would be avenged.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.750
Whispers slithered through the taverns and
back alleys of Flea Bottom.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:21.110
Two men were found; one was a former gold
cloak, the other a rat catcher in the Red

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.959
Keep who knew all its secrets.

00:02:23.959 --> 00:02:28.920
History remembers them only as Blood and Cheese.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:33.319
One night, Queen Helaena entered the royal
apartments with her daughter and two sons

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.030
to put them to bed.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.430
Without warning, Blood and Cheese burst in,
daggers in hand.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.489
They told her that a debt was owed.

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:43.840
A son for a son.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.060
Viserys: Rhaenyra's forces struck yet another
blow.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.200
The moment the Lord of Harrenhal saw Daemon
Targaryen circling the castle on his dragon

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.730
Caraxes, he struck his banners and surrendered.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:58.080
The Blacks now had the strongest castle in
the Riverlands.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.000
Robert: After Rook's Rest, Aemond One-Eye
took command of the Greens from his crippled

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.870
and poppy-addled brother.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:10.090
Aemond was the blood of the dragon, and dragons
don't cower behind city walls.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:15.800
He marched the king's army north to take back
Harrenhal from Rhaenyra's husband, Daemon.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:22.010
But when he and Criston Cole reached the castle,
they found the gates open, with Daemon and

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.010
all his men gone.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:30.110
That night they feasted their victory; Daemon
had fled rather than face their wrath.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:33.790
But Daemon was more snake than dragon.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:40.120
As Aemond marched north, he'd flown Caraxes
south, slithering past the Green army over

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.560
the waters of the Gods Eye.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.920
One day King's Landing looked up and saw two
dragons circling their foul city.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:53.840
Daemon and Rhaenyra had come for her throne,
for the city was defenseless.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:04:01.000
Aemond had taken the king's army from the
city, and worse, he'd taken his dragon Vhagar.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:06.410
Seeing that resistance was hopeless, the small
council surrendered the city, the Queen Mother

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.519
Alicent, and the broken Queen Helaena.

00:04:09.519 --> 00:04:12.120
But not King Aegon.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:17.730
Somehow, despite his wounds and delirium,
he had vanished from the city.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:23.760
Viserys: When a new army of Green loyalists
marched up from the Reach and laid siege to

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:28.830
the city of Tumbleton, Rhaenyra sent two of
her dragonseeds to lay waste to them.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:33.080
Instead, the dragonseeds proved their bastard
nature and betrayed her.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:37.830
They burned the city and all the Black forces
garrisoned within.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:43.530
Lucky for her, they didn't turn towards King's
Landing but drank in the ruins with the Greens,

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:46.530
who were victorious and somewhat confused.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:52.440
Oberyn Martell: Rhaenyra now mistrusted all
the dragonseeds, including the girl who rode

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.080
with her husband Daemon, hunting Aemond in
the Riverlands.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:00.020
She ordered the girl's head be sent to her.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:04.390
But there was a complication.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:08.780
As well as her dragon, the girl had taken
to riding Daemon.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:13.600
When Daemon received the queen's order, he
proclaimed it a queen's words and a work.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:18.890
He sent the girl away at dawn, watching her
and her dragon vanish into the morning mists.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:27.010
Then Daemon sent a challenge to his nephew
Aemond and flew to Harrenhal alone to wait.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:32.260
Fourteen days later, a shadow blacker than
any passing cloud swept over Harrenhal.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:38.490
Vhagar had come at last and on her rode one-eyed
Prince Aemond.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:40.490
He mocked Daemon for facing him alone.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:43.320
"You have lived too long, uncle."

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.940
And Daemon replied, "On that much, we agree."

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:52.270
Then the old prince climbed stiffly onto the
back of his dragon Caraxes but neglected to

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.760
fasten the chains that secured rider to saddle.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:01.190
The sun was close to setting when, as one,
the two dragons leapt into the sky.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:05.370
Daemon took Caraxes up swiftly until he disappeared
into a bank of clouds.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:08.570
Vhagar, older and slower, ascended more gradually.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:13.190
Up and up, Vhagar soared, searching for Caraxes.

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:17.180
Sudden as a thunderbolt, a shrieking Caraxes
dove upon Vhagar.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:20.710
Locked together, the dragons tumbled toward
the lake.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:25.021
Caraxes' jaws closed upon Vhagar's neck, but
Vhagar ripped open Caraxes's belly, and her

00:06:25.021 --> 00:06:27.020
teeth ripped off a wing.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:30.080
The lake rushed up with terrible speed.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:35.650
Then Daemon Targaryen, who had never fastened
his riding chains, stood in his saddle.

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:41.460
He leapt from his dragon to Aemond's, and
in his hand was Dark Sister, the Valyrian

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:44.850
sword of Aegon's sister-queen Visenya.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:49.970
As Aemond One-Eye looked up in terror, Daemon
ripped off his nephew's helm and drove the

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:56.190
sword down into his one remaining eye so hard
the point came out the back of the young prince's

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.190
throat.

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:02.350
Half a heartbeat later, the dragons struck
the lake, sending up a gout of water so high

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:11.160
that it was said to have been as tall as Harrenhal's
great tower.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.370
The lake boiled with dragon blood and then
was still.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:17.380
Daemon Targaryen was nine-and-forty at his
death.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:20.200
Prince Aemond had only turned twenty.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:28.530
Vhagar, the greatest of the Targaryen dragons,
had counted one-hundred-and-eighty-one years.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:32.980
Thus passed the last living creature from
the days of Aegon's Conquest.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:39.540
Viserys: Back in King's Landing, Queen Rhaenyra
didn't have much time to grieve for her stupid

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:40.540
husband.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:44.670
The mad former queen Helaena flung herself
from a balcony, to be impaled upon the iron

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.360
spikes lining the moat of Maegor's Holdfast.

